## Top-level application[¶](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com#top-level-application)

First, create the main, top-level, **FastAPI** application, and its *path operations*:

```
from fastapi import FastAPI
app = FastAPI()
@app.get("/app")
def read_main():
    return {"message": "Hello World from main app"}
subapi = FastAPI()
@subapi.get("/sub")
def read_sub():
    return {"message": "Hello World from sub API"}
app.mount("/subapi", subapi)
```

## Sub-application[¶](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com#sub-application)

Then, create your sub-application, and its *path operations*.

This sub-application is just another standard FastAPI application, but this is the one that will be "mounted":

```
from fastapi import FastAPI
app = FastAPI()
@app.get("/app")
def read_main():
    return {"message": "Hello World from main app"}
subapi = FastAPI()
@subapi.get("/sub")
def read_sub():
    return {"message": "Hello World from sub API"}
app.mount("/subapi", subapi)
```

## Mount the sub-application[¶](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com#mount-the-sub-application)

In your top-level application, `app`, mount the sub-application, `subapi`.

In this case, it will be mounted at the path `/subapi`:

```
from fastapi import FastAPI
app = FastAPI()
@app.get("/app")
def read_main():
    return {"message": "Hello World from main app"}
subapi = FastAPI()
@subapi.get("/sub")
def read_sub():
    return {"message": "Hello World from sub API"}
app.mount("/subapi", subapi)
```

